ildren":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"atoms"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSX.Element"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSX.Element"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"deprecated","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read table APIs or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms"},{"type":"text","value":" directly inside JSX,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMemo"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createEffect"},{"type":"text","value":". Solid tracks those reads natively.\nThis compatibility wrapper only passes atoms to its child function;\nit does not create a subscription or tracking scope."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfeatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFeatures"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableFeatures"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tdata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RowData"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-alias-solidtabletfeatures-tdata","text":"Type Alias: SolidTable<TFeatures, TData>","level":1},{"id":"type-declaration","text":"Type Declaration","level":2},{"id":"flexrender","text":"FlexRender","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"subscribe","text":"Subscribe","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"props","text":"props","level":5},{"id":"children","text":"children","level":6},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"deprecated","text":"Deprecated","level":4},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfeatures","text":"TFeatures","level":3},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Type Alias: SolidTable\\<TFeatures, TData\\>\n\n```ts\ntype SolidTable<TFeatures, TData> = Table<TFeatures, TData> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [createTable.ts:19](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/solid-table/src/createTable.ts#L19)\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### FlexRender\n\n```ts\nFlexRender: typeof FlexRender;\n```\n\nConvenience FlexRender component attached to the table instance for\nrendering headers, cells, or footers with custom markup. Mirrors the\n`table.FlexRender` API exposed by `createTableHook`'s `createAppTable`.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n<table.FlexRender header={header} />\n<table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n<table.FlexRender footer={footer} />\n```\n\n### ~~Subscribe~~\n\n```ts\nSubscribe: (props) => JSX.Element;\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### props\n\n###### children\n\n(`atoms`) => `JSX.Element`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`JSX.Element`\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nRead table APIs or `table.atoms` directly inside JSX,\n`createMemo`, or `createEffect`. Solid tracks those reads natively.\nThis compatibility wrapper only passes atoms to its child function;\nit does not create a subscription or tracking scope.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* `TableFeatures`\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* `RowData`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: SolidTable\ntitle: SolidTable\n---\n\n# Type Alias: SolidTable\\<TFeatures, TData\\>\n\n```ts\ntype SolidTable<TFeatures, TData> = Table<TFeatures, TData> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [createTable.ts:19](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/solid-table/src/createTable.ts#L19)\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### FlexRender\n\n```ts\nFlexRender: typeof FlexRender;\n```\n\nConvenience FlexRender component attached to the table instance for\nrendering headers, cells, or footers with custom markup. Mirrors the\n`table.FlexRender` API exposed by `createTableHook`'s `createAppTable`.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n<table.FlexRender header={header} />\n<table.FlexRender cell={cell} />\n<table.FlexRender footer={footer} />\n```\n\n### ~~Subscribe~~\n\n```ts\nSubscribe: (props) => JSX.Element;\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### props\n\n###### children\n\n(`atoms`) => `JSX.Element`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`JSX.Element`\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nRead table APIs or `table.atoms` directly inside JSX,\n`createMemo`, or `createEffect`. Solid tracks those reads natively.\nThis compatibility wrapper only passes atoms to its child function;\nit does not create a subscription or tracking scope.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* `TableFeatures`\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* `RowData`\n"}
